## SPECIFIC PROJECT RULES

### Todo Feature
- Todos have: id, title, description, completed, priority, dueDate, timestamps
- Priority levels: 'low', 'medium', 'high'
- Implement proper filtering and sorting
- Use optimistic updates for better UX
- Implement proper validation

### Database Schema
- Use PostgreSQL as primary database
- Implement proper migrations
- Use TypeORM for ORM
- Implement proper indexing
- Use transactions for data integrity

### Frontend State Management
- Use React Context for global state
- Use local state for component-specific state
- Implement proper loading states
- Handle error states gracefully
- Use optimistic updates

### API Integration
- Use Axios for HTTP requests
- Implement proper error handling
- Use interceptors for common headers
- Implement request/response logging
- Use proper timeout configurations

## COMMON PITFALLS TO AVOID

### Backend Pitfalls
- Don't expose sensitive data in responses
- Don't use synchronous operations for I/O
- Don't ignore error handling
- Don't use hardcoded values
- Don't skip input validation

### Frontend Pitfalls
- Don't mutate state directly
- Don't ignore loading states
- Don't forget error boundaries
- Don't use inline styles
- Don't ignore accessibility

### Shared Pitfalls
- Don't create circular dependencies
- Don't export everything from index files
- Don't ignore type safety
- Don't use any types unnecessarily
- Don't forget backward compatibility

